    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p45-q27-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_{-4\\pi}^{4\\pi}\\sin 3x\\,dx$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$",
          "worked": "$\\sin 3x$ is odd and the limits are symmetric about zero.\n$$\\int_{-4\\pi}^{4\\pi}\\sin 3x\\,dx=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q27-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_{-2\\pi}^{2\\pi}\\cos^2x\\sin^3x\\,dx$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$",
          "worked": "$\\cos^2x$ is even and $\\sin^3x$ is odd, so their product is odd. The limits are symmetric about zero.\n$$\\int_{-2\\pi}^{2\\pi}\\cos^2x\\sin^3x\\,dx=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q27-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_{-5\\pi/2}^{5\\pi/2}\\cos x\\,dx$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$",
          "worked": "$\\cos x$ is even.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int_{-5\\pi/2}^{5\\pi/2}\\cos x\\,dx&=2\\int_0^{5\\pi/2}\\cos x\\,dx\\\\&=2[\\sin x]_0^{5\\pi/2}\\\\&=2\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\\right)\\\\&=2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q27-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi}\\sec^2\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\,dx$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6\\sqrt3$",
          "worked": "$\\sec^2(\\frac{x}{3})$ is even.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi}\\sec^2\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\,dx&=2\\int_0^\\pi\\sec^2\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\,dx\\\\&=2\\left[3\\tan\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\right]_0^\\pi\\\\&=6\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\\\\&=6\\sqrt3.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q27-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi}(3+2x+\\sin x)\\,dx$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6\\pi$",
          "worked": "$2x$ and $\\sin x$ are odd, so each contributes zero over these symmetric limits. The constant function $3$ is even.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi}(3+2x+\\sin x)\\,dx&=2\\int_0^\\pi3\\,dx\\\\&=2[3x]_0^\\pi\\\\&=6\\pi.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q27-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2}(\\sin 2x+\\cos 3x+3x^2)\\,dx$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{\\pi^3}{4}-\\frac23$",
          "worked": "$\\sin 2x$ is odd, so it contributes zero. Both $\\cos 3x$ and $3x^2$ are even.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\cos 3x\\,dx&=2\\left[\\frac13\\sin 3x\\right]_0^{\\pi/2}\\\\&=\\frac23(-1)\\\\&=-\\frac23.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\int_0^{\\pi/2}3x^2\\,dx&=[2x^3]_0^{\\pi/2}\\\\&=\\frac{\\pi^3}{4}.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2}(\\sin 2x+\\cos 3x+3x^2)\\,dx=-\\frac23+\\frac{\\pi^3}{4}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
